blocks.english:
He pours forth prayers and canticles,
Bending his knees in piety;
In music so pleasing to God
The heavenly ones themselves rejoice;

In the first season of youth
He refused to cling to trifles;
With manly strength of mind
He beheld Circe driven away;

He tames fires and seas,
Earth and the winds of the air;
His tongue gives speech to the mute,
And to the blind the use of sight;
